      "id": 1,
      "text": "Heckscherville got its name when the Heckscher family bought the Payne brothers’ holdings and renamed the Irish‑named valley after themselves.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heckscherville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1831 the entire Heckscherville valley consisted of just two villages.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heckscherville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the 1845 Irish famine, the Payne brothers lured hundreds of families from Kilkenny and Queens counties to settle in the valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heckscherville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Kear’s Hill and Green Hill vanished as coal mining pushed them out of the valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heckscherville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Heckscherville sits between Broad Mountain to the north and the Thomaston/Mine Hill range to the west.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heckscherville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
